// APW-2 — Approval replay (approval never consumed) — BUGGY variant.
//
// The same intent as the correct variant ("order only after the cart has been
// confirmed"), but the `since` clause is *absent*: nothing consumes the
// cart-check. One `get_cart::response` therefore authorises EVERY matching
// `place_order` in the window — a parallel burst of N orders, all matching
// that single cart-check, are all admitted (one verification authorises N
// actions).
//
// The one-clause bug vs. the correct variant: no `since` suffix, so the gated
// action is a bare negated event reference (a replayable trigger).
//
// Schema: Drupe namespace.
// See: rot/shapes.py (build_approval_replay_ir -- the hand-written oracle),
//      samples/reference/apw2-order-after-cart-check-buggy.dw (verbatim source).
@id("approval_replay_buggy")
forbid (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"PlaceOrder",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    !Drupe::Action::"PlaceOrder"::response{ input.amount: context.input.amount }
};